---
// src/pages/quant.astro — The Quant Path, a learning-in-public syllabus
import Analytics from '../components/Analytics.astro';
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta name="description" content="From ML engineer to quant — the honest, learning-in-public syllabus Austin Nafe is working through: time series, microstructure, econometrics, and backtesting without fooling yourself.">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">
  <meta property="og:title" content="The Quant Path — a working syllabus">
  <meta property="og:description" content="From ML engineer to quant, learning in public: the curriculum and the project.">
  <meta property="og:image" content="/profile.jpg">
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
  <title>The Quant Path — a working syllabus · Austin Nafe</title>
  <style is:global>
  :root {
    --ink: #080e12; --bg: #0c1419; --surface: #14202a; --surface-2: #1d2c39;
    --border: #26384a; --border-bright: #38516a;
    --text: #e8eef2; --dim: #93a4b0; --mute: #5f7280;
    --gold: #d4af37; --gold-soft: #e6c65c; --green: #3bab77; --red: #d0684f;
    --sans: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", system-ui, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    --mono: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", "JetBrains Mono", Menlo, Monaco, monospace;
    --rail-w: 252px; --maxw: 860px;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
  body {
    background: radial-gradient(1100px 640px at 80% -10%, rgba(212,175,55,0.09), transparent 60%), var(--bg);
    color: var(--text); font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.62; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  ::selection { background: rgba(212,175,55,0.3); color: #fff; }
  a { color: var(--gold); text-decoration: none; } a:hover { color: var(--gold-soft); }
  :focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--gold); outline-offset: 3px; border-radius: 3px; }

  .shell { display: flex; }
  .rail { position: sticky; top: 0; align-self: flex-start; width: var(--rail-w); height: 100vh; flex-shrink: 0; padding: 30px 22px; border-right: 1px solid var(--border); background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(8,14,18,0.7), rgba(8,14,18,0.2)); backdrop-filter: blur(6px); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; z-index: 20; }
  .rail-brand { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--dim); }
  .rail-brand b { color: var(--text); font-weight: 700; font-size: 15px; display: block; margin-top: 3px; text-transform: none; letter-spacing: 0.01em; }
  .rail-brand i { color: var(--mute); font-style: normal; font-size: 10.5px; display: block; margin-top: 2px; }
  .rail-list { list-style: none; margin-top: 18px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1px; overflow-y: auto; }
  .rail-item { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--mute); padding: 6px 9px; border-radius: 7px; cursor: pointer; transition: color .2s, background .2s; border-left: 2px solid transparent; width: 100%; text-align: left; background: none; }
  .rail-item:hover { color: var(--dim); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); }
  .rail-item .rn { color: var(--mute); font-size: 10.5px; width: 18px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .rail-item.active { color: var(--text); background: rgba(212,175,55,0.09); border-left-color: var(--gold); }
  .rail-item.active .rn { color: var(--gold); }
  .rail-item.done .rn { color: var(--green); }
  .rail-div { margin-top: 14px; padding: 2px 9px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.13em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--mute); }
  .rail-foot { margin-top: auto; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10.5px; color: var(--mute); line-height: 1.6; padding-top: 12px; }

  main { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
  .panel { min-height: 100vh; padding: 84px clamp(24px, 6vw, 88px); display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .panel-inner { width: 100%; max-width: var(--maxw); margin: 0 auto; }

  .eyebrow { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12.5px; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .eyebrow::before { content: ""; width: 24px; height: 1px; background: var(--gold); opacity: .6; }
  .eyebrow .n { color: var(--mute); }

  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 5.4vw, 4rem); line-height: 1.04; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.025em; text-wrap: balance; }
  h2 { font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3.6vw, 2.5rem); line-height: 1.08; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.022em; text-wrap: balance; }
  .lede { font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.7vw, 1.24rem); color: var(--dim); max-width: 64ch; margin-top: 18px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .lede strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
  p.body { color: var(--dim); max-width: 66ch; margin-top: 14px; } p.body strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
  em { color: var(--text); font-style: italic; }
  .gold { color: var(--gold-soft); } .grn { color: var(--green); } .rd { color: var(--red); }

  .reveal { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(18px); transition: opacity .6s ease, transform .6s ease; }
  .reveal.in { opacity: 1; transform: none; }

  #hero { justify-content: center; }
  .hero-kicker { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12.5px; letter-spacing: 0.13em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--dim); margin-bottom: 22px; display:flex; gap:12px; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:center; }
  .hero h1 .g { background: linear-gradient(100deg, var(--gold) 20%, var(--gold-soft) 60%, #f0e0a0 95%); -webkit-background-clip: text; background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero-cta { margin-top: 34px; display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .btn { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; padding: 11px 18px; border-radius: 9px; border: 1px solid var(--border-bright); color: var(--text); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02); cursor: pointer; transition: all .2s; display:inline-flex; gap:8px; align-items:center; }
  .btn.primary { background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--gold), #b8942a); border-color: var(--gold); color: #1a1305; font-weight: 700; }
  .btn:hover { border-color: var(--gold); color: var(--gold-soft); } .btn.primary:hover { filter: brightness(1.06); color:#1a1305; }
  .scroll-hint { margin-top: 40px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--mute); display:flex; gap:10px; align-items:center; }
  .scroll-hint .k { border:1px solid var(--border-bright); border-radius:5px; padding:2px 7px; color: var(--dim); }

  /* have/skip list */
  .cols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; margin-top: 30px; }
  .col { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 14px; padding: 22px; background: var(--surface); }
  .col .ct { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 14px; display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; }
  .col.have .ct { color: var(--green); } .col.gap .ct { color: var(--gold); }
  .col ul { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 9px; }
  .col li { font-size: 0.96rem; color: var(--dim); padding-left: 20px; position: relative; }
  .col.have li::before { content: "✓"; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--green); font-weight: 700; }
  .col.gap li::before { content: "→"; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--gold); font-weight: 700; }
  .col li b { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }

  /* module */
  .mod-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 16px; }
  .mod-num { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 2.4rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--gold); line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .mod-tag { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--mute); }
  .mgrid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 18px; margin-top: 26px; }
  .mcard { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 13px; padding: 20px; background: var(--surface); }
  .mcard .ml { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.09em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold); margin-bottom: 11px; display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; }
  .mcard p { color: var(--dim); font-size: 0.95rem; } .mcard p b { color: var(--text); }
  .topics { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 7px; margin-top: 4px; }
  .topic { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; padding: 5px 10px; border-radius: 7px; border: 1px solid var(--border-bright); color: var(--dim); }
  .why { margin-top: 24px; border-left: 3px solid var(--gold); padding: 4px 0 4px 20px; font-size: 1.06rem; color: var(--text); }
  .why .wl { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold); display:block; margin-bottom: 7px; }
  .resource { margin-top: 16px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--mute); } .resource b { color: var(--dim); font-weight: 600; }

  /* project */
  .proj-box { margin-top: 26px; border: 1px solid var(--border-bright); border-radius: 16px; padding: 26px; background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(212,175,55,0.06), transparent); }
  .steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(150px,1fr)); gap: 12px; margin-top: 20px; }
  .step { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 11px; padding: 15px; background: var(--surface); }
  .step .sn { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--gold); } .step .st { font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 5px 0 3px; } .step .sd { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--mute); }

  /* resources */
  .res-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 18px; margin-top: 26px; }
  .res { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 13px; padding: 20px; background: var(--surface); }
  .res h3 { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--gold); font-family: var(--mono); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .res ul { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 9px; }
  .res li { font-size: 0.93rem; color: var(--dim); } .res li b { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }

  .callout { margin-top: 26px; border: 1px dashed var(--border-bright); border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px 20px; font-size: 0.98rem; color: var(--dim); }
  .callout b { color: var(--text); }
  #close { text-align: center; } #close .panel-inner { display:flex; flex-direction: column; align-items:center; }
  .close-links { display:flex; gap: 12px; margin-top: 28px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content:center; }
  .aifoot { margin-top: 34px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--mute); max-width: 58ch; line-height: 1.75; text-align:center; }

  .progress { position: fixed; top: 0; left: var(--rail-w); right: 0; height: 2px; z-index: 40; }
  .progress i { display:block; height:100%; width:0%; background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--gold), var(--green)); transition: width .1s linear; }

  @media (max-width: 920px) { .rail { display:none; } .progress { left:0; } main { width:100%; } .cols, .mgrid, .res-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .panel { padding: 70px 22px; } body { font-size: 16px; } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { * { transition-duration:.001ms !important; } html { scroll-behavior:auto; } .reveal { opacity:1; transform:none; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>


<div class="progress"><i id="progBar"></i></div>

<div class="shell">
  <nav class="rail" aria-label="Contents">
    <div class="rail-brand">Austin Nafe<b>The Quant Path</b><i>A working syllabus · learning in public</i></div>
    <ul class="rail-list" id="railList">
      <li><button class="rail-item" data-goto="hero"><span class="rn">00</span> The plan</button></li>
      <li><button class="rail-item" data-goto="start"><span class="rn">01</span> Where I'm starting</button></li>
      <li class="rail-div">The gaps — my curriculum</li>
      <li><button class="rail-item" data-goto="m1"><span class="rn">M1</span> Time series</button></li>
      <li><button class="rail-item" data-goto="m2"><span class="rn">M2</span> Microstructure</button></li>
      <li><button class="rail-item" data-goto="m3"><span class="rn">M3</span> Econometrics</button></li>
      <li><button class="rail-item" data-goto="m4"><span class="rn">M4</span> Portfolio &amp; risk</button></li>
      <li><button class="rail-item" data-goto="m5"><span class="rn">M5</span> Not fooling myself</button></li>
      <li class="rail-div">Do the work</li>
      <li><button class="rail-item" data-goto="project"><span class="rn">02</span> The project</button></li>
      <li><button class="rail-item" data-goto="resources"><span class="rn">03</span> Resources</button></li>
    </ul>
    <div class="rail-foot"><a href="/">← Back to portfolio</a><br><a href="/intelligence">Austin's Intelligence</a></div>
  </nav>

  <main>
    <!-- HERO -->
    <section class="panel" id="hero" data-rung="hero">
      <div class="panel-inner">
        <div class="hero-kicker"><span>Learning in public</span><span style="color:var(--mute)">· updated as I go</span></div>
        <h1>From ML engineer to <span class="g">quant.</span><br>The syllabus I'm actually working through.</h1>
        <p class="lede">I have the CS, the finance degree, and the ML — so I'm not starting at zero, and I'm not pretending to be a hedge-fund quant either. This is the honest curriculum for the part I <em>don't</em> have yet: turning statistical skill into an <strong>exploitable edge, after costs.</strong> Public, so I can't quietly skip the hard parts.</p>
        <div class="hero-cta">
          <button class="btn primary" data-goto="start">See the plan ↓</button>
          <a class="btn" href="/">Portfolio</a>
        </div>
        <div class="scroll-hint"><span class="k">↓</span> scroll, or <span class="k">→</span> to move module to module</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- START -->
    <section class="panel" id="start" data-rung="start">
      <div class="panel-inner reveal">
        <div class="eyebrow"><span class="n">01</span> Where I'm starting</div>
        <h2>Skip what I already have; spend the time on the gaps.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Most "learn quant" roadmaps start with a statistics month I've already done. The point of a syllabus is to be honest about that — and put the hours where they actually move me.</p>
        <div class="cols">
          <div class="col have">
            <div class="ct">Already have — don't re-learn</div>
            <ul>
              <li><b>CS + finance degrees</b>, master's in CS</li>
              <li><b>ML engineering</b> — the overfitting instinct is the real asset</li>
              <li>Hypothesis testing, regression, Bayesian thinking</li>
              <li>Distributions, covariance, PCA, <b>factor models</b> (statistically)</li>
              <li>Python — pandas, numpy, the whole stack</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="col gap">
            <div class="ct">The gaps — where the hours go</div>
            <ul>
              <li><b>Time series</b> — the least-transferable from general ML</li>
              <li><b>Market microstructure</b> — how markets actually fill</li>
              <li><b>Financial econometrics</b> — stats applied to returns</li>
              <li><b>Portfolio construction</b> — sizing and risk</li>
              <li><b>Backtesting rigor</b> — not fooling myself</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="callout"><b>The destination, honestly:</b> not PhD quant research. It's <span class="gold">AI × finance</span> — quant development and financial ML, which extend what I already do rather than reset it. Independent trading is the sandbox I learn in, not an income plan — the payoff is the skillset.</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- M1 TIME SERIES -->
    <section class="panel" id="m1" data-rung="m1">
      <div class="panel-inner reveal">
        <div class="mod-head"><span class="mod-num">M1</span><div><div class="mod-tag">Module · biggest delta</div><h2>Time series</h2></div></div>
        <div class="mgrid">
          <div class="mcard">
            <div class="ml">What I'm learning</div>
            <div class="topics"><span class="topic">stationarity</span><span class="topic">autocorrelation</span><span class="topic">ARIMA</span><span class="topic">GARCH</span><span class="topic">cointegration</span><span class="topic">Kalman filters</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="mcard">
            <div class="ml">In one line</div>
            <p>General ML assumes your data is drawn from a fixed distribution. Markets aren't — the pattern <b>drifts over time</b>. Time series is the toolkit for data that won't sit still.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="why"><span class="wl">Why it matters</span>Most tradable signals — momentum, mean reversion, pairs — <em>are</em> time-series structure. This is the module that's genuinely new coming from ML, so it gets the most time.</div>
        <div class="resource"><b>Resource:</b> Hilpisch, <em>Python for Algorithmic Trading</em> · statsmodels docs · a cointegration walk-through on a real pair</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- M2 MICROSTRUCTURE -->
    <section class="panel" id="m2" data-rung="m2">
      <div class="panel-inner reveal">
        <div class="mod-head"><span class="mod-num">M2</span><div><div class="mod-tag">Module · the reality check</div><h2>Market microstructure</h2></div></div>
        <div class="mgrid">
          <div class="mcard">
            <div class="ml">What I'm learning</div>
            <div class="topics"><span class="topic">order books</span><span class="topic">bid/ask spread</span><span class="topic">slippage</span><span class="topic">liquidity</span><span class="topic">market makers</span><span class="topic">execution</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="mcard">
            <div class="ml">In one line</div>
            <p>How trades <b>actually fill</b> — and why the price in your backtest isn't the price you'd get. This is the difference between a strategy on paper and a strategy that survives contact with a real market.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="why"><span class="wl">Why it matters</span>Ignoring costs and slippage is the #1 way a backtest lies. You can't judge an edge until you know what crossing the spread costs you.</div>
        <div class="resource"><b>Resource:</b> Larry Harris, <em>Trading and Exchanges</em> — the standard text</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- M3 ECONOMETRICS -->
    <section class="panel" id="m3" data-rung="m3">
      <div class="panel-inner reveal">
        <div class="mod-head"><span class="mod-num">M3</span><div><div class="mod-tag">Module · adapting what I know</div><h2>Financial econometrics</h2></div></div>
        <div class="mgrid">
          <div class="mcard">
            <div class="ml">What I'm learning</div>
            <div class="topics"><span class="topic">CAPM</span><span class="topic">Fama–French factors</span><span class="topic">alpha / beta</span><span class="topic">volatility modeling</span><span class="topic">heteroskedasticity</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="mcard">
            <div class="ml">In one line</div>
            <p>I know factor models as statistics; here they're <b>applied to returns</b>. The reframe: from "does this feature improve accuracy?" to "does this factor explain <em>returns</em>, and is the alpha real?"</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="why"><span class="wl">Why it matters</span>This is the shortest module for me — the stats transfer directly. The work is the vocabulary and the framing, not new math.</div>
        <div class="resource"><b>Resource:</b> Ernest Chan, <em>Algorithmic Trading</em> · López de Prado for the ML crossover</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- M4 PORTFOLIO -->
    <section class="panel" id="m4" data-rung="m4">
      <div class="panel-inner reveal">
        <div class="mod-head"><span class="mod-num">M4</span><div><div class="mod-tag">Module · sizing &amp; risk</div><h2>Portfolio construction</h2></div></div>
        <div class="mgrid">
          <div class="mcard">
            <div class="ml">What I'm learning</div>
            <div class="topics"><span class="topic">mean–variance</span><span class="topic">risk parity</span><span class="topic">Kelly criterion</span><span class="topic">convex optimization</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="mcard">
            <div class="ml">In one line</div>
            <p>Optimization I know — but pointed at <b>how much to bet and how to spread risk</b>, not at training a model. Finding an edge is half the job; sizing it without blowing up is the other half.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="why"><span class="wl">Why it matters</span>A mediocre signal sized well beats a great signal sized recklessly. Risk management is where most independent traders actually fail.</div>
        <div class="resource"><b>Resource:</b> convex optimization refresher · Kelly-criterion derivation by hand</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- M5 NOT FOOLING MYSELF -->
    <section class="panel" id="m5" data-rung="m5">
      <div class="panel-inner reveal">
        <div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--red)"><span class="n" style="color:var(--red);opacity:.7">M5 · the whole game</span> Not fooling myself</div>
        <h2>My ML background is an edge here — and a trap.</h2>
        <p class="lede"><strong>The edge:</strong> I already understand overfitting and cross-validation, so "is this signal real or noise?" is a question I know how to ask. <strong>The trap:</strong> financial data breaks the assumptions ML trained me on — it's <span class="rd">non-stationary</span>, the signal-to-noise is <span class="rd">brutally low</span>, and you get <span class="rd">one history</span> to test on. It's trivially easy to p-hack a beautiful backtest that's pure overfitting.</p>
        <div class="mgrid" style="margin-top:22px">
          <div class="mcard">
            <div class="ml" style="color:var(--red)">The ways I'll fool myself</div>
            <div class="topics"><span class="topic">lookahead bias</span><span class="topic">survivorship bias</span><span class="topic">multiple testing</span><span class="topic">ignoring costs</span><span class="topic">regime change</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="mcard">
            <div class="ml">The discipline</div>
            <p>Out-of-sample everything. Cost and slippage in <b>every</b> backtest. Count how many strategies you tried before the one that "worked." Assume the edge decays.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="why" style="border-left-color:var(--red)"><span class="wl" style="color:var(--red)">The one book</span>López de Prado, <em>Advances in Financial Machine Learning</em> — it's specifically about applying ML to markets <em>without</em> these traps. This is the module that separates people who make money from people who overfit.</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- PROJECT -->
    <section class="panel" id="project" data-rung="project">
      <div class="panel-inner reveal">
        <div class="eyebrow"><span class="n">02</span> Do the work</div>
        <h2>Don't read for six months. Build one backtest and watch it fail.</h2>
        <p class="lede">The fastest way to learn quant research is to test a real hypothesis, honestly, and figure out <em>why</em> it doesn't work. One rigorous backtest teaches more than three months of books — so the project comes early, not last.</p>
        <div class="proj-box">
          <div style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold)">The build · a rigorous backtester + one strategy</div>
          <div class="steps">
            <div class="step"><div class="sn">01</div><div class="st">Pick one strategy</div><div class="sd">Momentum or mean-reversion. Simple on purpose.</div></div>
            <div class="step"><div class="sn">02</div><div class="st">Backtest it honestly</div><div class="sd">Real OHLCV, transaction costs, no lookahead.</div></div>
            <div class="step"><div class="sn">03</div><div class="st">Watch it fail</div><div class="sd">Most do. Sharpe, drawdown, why it broke.</div></div>
            <div class="step"><div class="sn">04</div><div class="st">Iterate</div><div class="sd">Repeat until I can tell a real edge from noise.</div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="resource" style="margin-top:16px"><b>Tools:</b> vectorbt or backtesting.py · pandas / numpy · one weekend to the first failed backtest</div>
        </div>
        <div class="callout"><b>The real goal</b> isn't to get rich — it's to become someone who can <span class="gold">systematically evaluate a trading hypothesis</span>. That skill pays off in quant-dev, risk analytics, and financial-AI roles even if I never trade a live dollar.</div>
